 "summary_html": "<p>In book design, the <b>author page</b> is a section of a book or other literary work that consists of a short—usually a single page long—biography of the author, sometimes accompanied by a photograph of them. Written in the third-person narrative, this page is usually entitled \"about the author\", resulting in the synonymous name \"<b>about the author page</b>\". The author page appears in the back matter of a book, usually as the final page; thus, it does not possess a page number. However, in print, it may be followed by the flyleaf.</p>",
 "summary_text": "In book design, the author page is a section of a book or other literary work that consists of a short—usually a single page long—biography of the author, sometimes accompanied by a photograph of them. Written in the third-person narrative, this page is usually entitled \"about the author\", resulting in the synonymous name \"about the author page\". The author page appears in the back matter of a book, usually as the final page; thus, it does not possess a page number. However, in print, it may be followed by the flyleaf.",
